[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports show three
problems. The parser fix repairs one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket and its own fix.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/navamara55/megadev-w1-c3-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/navamara55/megadev-w1-c3-what-it-shows/issues/2',
    'one-day': 'https://github.com/navamara55/megadev-w1-c3-what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day first,
  so day and month swap: 2 July becomes 7 February. This is what #4471 describes.
- **`hint`**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and reads the date
  day first. People type what the hint says. Only form reports from `booking-v3` tenants.
  Fixing the parser does not fix the form.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by one day, not day for month. The same meeting is Tuesday in
  Lisbon and Monday in Toronto. That is a time-zone conversion. The desk already noted these
  as a one-day move ([desk-notes](https://github.com/navamara55/megadev-w1-c3-what-it-shows/blob/main/src/lib/data/desk-notes.json)),
  but the #4471 table still counts them under `parser`.

## Why one ticket

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. Every
subject here says "wrong day" in some form, so every report landed in #4471. The cause depends
on the tenant, its booking form and the channel the report came through, and the subject says
none of that. Intake's tag guesses from the reporter's browser, so it does not settle it either.

## How the count works

One id, one report: the ticket export repeats some rows. Each report goes to one problem: a
report on the desk's one-day list is `one-day`; any other gets its cause from `causes.ts`.
The table is built from the export at render time.

